      "doc_id": "rbi-13141",
      "quote": "(1) maintain all necessary records of transactions between the bank and the customer, both domestic and international, for at least five years from the date of transaction;\n\n(2) preserve the records pertaining to the identification of the customers and their addresses, obtained while opening the account and during the course of business relationship, for at least five years after the business relationship has ended;"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "rationale": "The bank's policy preserves transaction records for ten years and customer identification records for five years. Since keeping records for a longer period is a stricter standard than the mandatory five-year minimum, the clause is compliant."
}
